# PROFILE_APEX swaps the domain every owner is resolved and linked under.
#
# Export it in the deploy's BUILD environment — not in a .env file here. Two
# reasons, and both bite silently. Owner pages prerender, so the school
# switcher's absolute links are baked in at build: setting it only where the
# server runs leaves the switcher pointing at production. And turbo hashes the
# variable, not the file: an ignored .env.local is not a build input, so a
# staging build that reads it matches production's hash and replays the cached
# artifact.
#
#   PROFILE_APEX=staging.example.com pnpm build

# Nothing else is required yet. The profile site renders from packages/school-config
# and does not call the API. When it starts reading admission facts, add
# API_BASE_URL here and a validated schema in src/config/env.ts, the way
# apps/api does it.
